| info = 
*Gyre expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' [[energy]] to deploy a Gyratory Sphere using an underhand throw with an arcing trajectory toward the aiming reticle. The Coil Horizon sphere is a physics-based object with a high initial velocity as it rebounds against surfaces and obstacles during its <u>'''2'''</u> second lifetime. Direct contact inflicts {{D|Knockdown}} and {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''1,000 / 1,150 / 1,300 / 1,500'''{{D|Electricity}} damage per second with <u>'''100%'''</u> [[Status Chance]].
**Gyre throws the sphere with her left hand, as such the object is not created directly in front of her and instead travels toward the left-half of the aiming reticle.
**Due to its physics object properties, Coil Horizon is attracted by {{A|Bastille}}'s vortex mode, {{A|Tornado}}, and other similar abilities.
*Upon reaching the end of its lifetime, or when manually triggered by pressing the ability key again (default {{Keybind|2}}), Coil Horizon detonates itself in an electromagnetic implosion spanning a {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''12''' meter radius that lingers for <u>'''2'''</u> seconds. Enemies in sight detection range are dealt {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''500 / 750 / 1,000 / 1,250''' {{D|Electricity}} damage with a guaranteed status effect. Affected enemies and any enemies that subsequently enter the implosion radius are rapidly pulled into its center in a {{D|Ragdoll}} state.
**Damage on implosion diminishes with distance from the center.
**The implosion can damage and break destructible [[Objects]], bypassing line-of-sight restriction in its range.
**Any [[Pickups]] that spawn from enemies killed and destructible objects broken by Coil Horizon are vacuumed to the center of the implosion. Regular items left on the ground are unaffected by the suction.
*Can be recast while active to detonate the sphere, or throw a new sphere while an implosion vortex exists.
*Casting and manually detonating Coil Horizon are upper-body animations that allow player movement and [[Maneuvers]] while restricting other actions.
*Gyre visually conjures an alternate Gyratory Sphere core in her left hand as she tosses it forward. The sphere rolls along in its deployed plated form emitting electric sparks until the implosion occurs, then warps the magnetic plates into outward-pointing triangular spikes that individually rotate. Void energy flares and an event horizon appear around the sphere's core, which gradually dissolves away.
| interactions = 
* Gyre's [[Gyre/Abilities#Passive|Passive]] and {{A|Cathode Grace}} enable ability [[Critical Hit]]s by granting <u>'''0%'''</u> to <u>'''300%'''</u> critical chance to damage and status effects dealt by Coil Horizon, which trigger lightning discharges from {{A|Rotorswell}}.
* Coil Horizon's enemy suction effect assists in {{A|Arcsphere}}'s damage enhancement.
* Direct kills by Coil Horizon, its {{D|Electricity}} status effects, and kill assists from allies extend Cathode Grace's duration.
| helminth = 
*Subsuming Gyre to the [[Helminth]] will offer Coil Horizon and its augments to be used by other Warframes.
